# The buildx and buildkit versions every build of the action's image uses.
#
# Both decide the bytes a build produces, so publishing and every rebuild that
# checks a published digest have to use the same ones. They live in a file
# rather than on the setup-buildx-action step that consumes them because they
# were once written out on three such steps, and the two workflows that did not
# declare them recovered them by parsing the one that did.
#
# .github/actions/setup-builder is that step now, and the only file under
# .github that reads this one. Read with script/builder-pins, which strips these
# comments.
#
# Neither pin is managed by Dependabot: the github-actions ecosystem bumps
# `uses:` SHAs, and the docker ecosystem reads the Dockerfile, so neither
# ecosystem can see a key=value file. script/bump-builder-pins is what moves
# them instead -- resolving the newest release of each and rewriting the two
# lines below -- run weekly by .github/workflows/bump-builder-pins.yml, which
# pushes a branch for review. A bump by hand is still just an edit here.
#
# A change here changes the image, so this file is on the build-input list in
# script/verify-digest.
#
# The buildkit pin says where it comes from, being an image reference. A bare
# version does not, so: buildx is released at github.com/docker/buildx, which is
# where script/bump-builder-pins reads it from and where a bump by hand should
# look.

BUILDKIT_IMAGE=moby/buildkit:v0.32.2@sha256:28a898719c18a33f4e8000685287fa36fd0dd9560c6440227d3a732d79bb41d8
BUILDX_VERSION=v0.36.1
